---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Selected Work" description="Selected work — Ben Muratet" noindex={true}>
  <div style="background:#111D35;padding:0.8rem 2rem;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
    <span style="font-size:0.62rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#B8922E">Unlisted &middot; Prepared for Dolby ATG</span>
    <a href="mailto:ben@benmuratet.com" style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;color:#E8E4DF">ben@benmuratet.com</a>
  </div>

  <div style="background:#FAF8F5;color:#1B2A4A;font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif">



    <section style="background:#111D35;color:#FAF8F5;padding:6rem 2rem 7rem;position:relative;overflow:hidden">
      <div style="position:absolute;right:-14rem;top:-10rem;width:44rem;height:44rem;border-radius:50%;background:radial-gradient(circle at 40% 40%, rgba(139,105,20,0.30), rgba(17,29,53,0) 68%);pointer-events:none"></div>
      <div style="max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,27rem),1fr));gap:3rem 4rem;align-items:start">
        <div>
          <p style="font-size:0.66rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#B8922E;margin:0 0 1.6rem">Ben Muratet &middot; Atlanta, GA</p>
          <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.15rem,4.2vw,3.6rem);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.045em;line-height:1.04;margin:0 0 1.8rem;max-width:20ch;text-wrap:balance">I stand between design and engineering &mdash; and build the thing that settles the argument.</h1>
          <p style="font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.62;color:#C9CFDB;margin:0 0 1.3rem;max-width:48ch;text-wrap:pretty">I manage the team that engineers client designs into buildable products: CNC prototyping, custom jigs and hold-downs, and delivery and installation from a single residential room to multi-day commercial builds. Physical systems and digital ones get built the same way &mdash; and I build both.</p>
          <p style="font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.62;color:#C9CFDB;margin:0;max-width:48ch;text-wrap:pretty">Before that, a decade of hands-on technical production: video routing and imaging monitoring on set, LED volume and virtual-production stages, Unreal Engine real-time camera tracking feeding VR/AR pipelines, cinematography and lighting. Real-time creative and technical calls, made under deadline, in front of the people paying for them.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.15rem;padding-bottom:0.4rem">
          <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(232,228,223,0.18);padding-top:1.15rem">
            <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B9AB5;margin-bottom:0.4rem">The loop, every time</div>
            <div style="font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.03em;color:#FAF8F5">Invent &middot; Prototype<br />Judge &middot; Repeat</div>
          </div>
          <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(232,228,223,0.18);padding-top:1.15rem">
            <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B9AB5;margin-bottom:0.6rem">Physical systems</div>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.35rem">
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(250,248,245,0.11);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">CNC prototyping</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(250,248,245,0.11);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">Jigs &amp; hold-downs</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(250,248,245,0.11);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">Delivery &amp; installation</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(250,248,245,0.11);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">Multi-day commercial builds</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="border-top:1px solid rgba(232,228,223,0.18);padding-top:1.15rem">
            <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B9AB5;margin-bottom:0.6rem">Real-time &amp; immersive</div>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.35rem">
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(184,146,46,0.22);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">LED volume stages</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(184,146,46,0.22);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">Unreal camera tracking</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(184,146,46,0.22);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">VR/AR pipelines</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(184,146,46,0.22);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">Video routing</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(184,146,46,0.22);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">Imaging monitoring</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:500;color:#E8E4DF;background:rgba(184,146,46,0.22);padding:0.28rem 0.7rem;border-radius:999px">Cinematography &amp; lighting</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="padding:3rem 2rem 2.6rem;background:#FAF8F5">
      <div style="max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,20rem),1fr));gap:2.5rem;align-items:start">
        <div>
          <p style="font-size:0.62rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B6914;margin:0 0 0.9rem">What follows</p>
          <p style="font-size:1.12rem;line-height:1.6;color:#1B2A4A;font-weight:500;margin:0;max-width:52ch;text-wrap:pretty">Four things I built and shipped when the tool that should have existed didn&rsquo;t. Different mediums, one method: read whether an idea works before it&rsquo;s finished, build the version that proves it, then say plainly what it proved.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.7rem;padding-top:0.3rem">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:0.9rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-size:0.66rem;font-weight:800;color:#8B6914;flex:none;width:1.5rem">01</span><span style="font-size:0.88rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.4"><strong style="color:#1B2A4A">OpenCraft</strong> &mdash; RFQ email to defensible quote, for a shop with no SKUs</span></div>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:0.9rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-size:0.66rem;font-weight:800;color:#8B6914;flex:none;width:1.5rem">02</span><span style="font-size:0.88rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.4"><strong style="color:#1B2A4A">Kabbalah Wave</strong> &mdash; generative CNC, taken to a physical cut</span></div>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:0.9rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-size:0.66rem;font-weight:800;color:#8B6914;flex:none;width:1.5rem">03</span><span style="font-size:0.88rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.4"><strong style="color:#1B2A4A">theoakhome.com</strong> &mdash; a brand built from a blank page, solo</span></div>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:0.9rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-size:0.66rem;font-weight:800;color:#8B6914;flex:none;width:1.5rem">04</span><span style="font-size:0.88rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.4"><strong style="color:#1B2A4A">Shop Floor Board</strong> &mdash; an ops tool in daily use on the floor</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="padding:3rem 2rem 5rem;background:#FAF8F5">
      <div style="max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto">

        <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:2rem;margin-bottom:2.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <div style="font-size:5.5rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.05em;line-height:0.8;color:rgba(27,42,74,0.11);flex:none">01</div>
          <div style="flex:1;min-width:min(100%,26rem)">
            <div style="font-size:0.62rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B6914;margin-bottom:0.7rem">Estimating Software &middot; In production since Feb 2026</div>
            <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.9rem,3.6vw,2.7rem);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.038em;line-height:1.05;margin:0 0 0.6rem;color:#1B2A4A;max-width:28ch">OpenCraft: estimating for a shop with no repeatable products</h2>
            <p style="font-size:1rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.6;margin:0;max-width:60ch">An RFQ email goes in. Line items come out, get matched against comparable past jobs by keyword, and run through a category-specific math engine &mdash; tabletops, desks, cabinetry and upholstery each have their own. Built from inside the trade, for the people doing the quoting.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="flex:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem;align-items:flex-start">
            <a href="https://opencraftapp.netlify.app/dashboard" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;background:#1B2A4A;color:#FAF8F5;font-size:0.76rem;font-weight:600;padding:0.6rem 1.1rem;border-radius:999px">Live dashboard &rarr;</a>
            <span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#4A5568">Product Designer, Full-Stack Dev</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="padding:1.6rem 1.8rem;background:rgba(139,105,20,0.07);border-left:4px solid #8B6914;border-radius:0 16px 16px 0;margin-bottom:2.4rem">
          <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B6914;margin-bottom:0.7rem">What it proves</div>
          <p style="margin:0;font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.5;color:#1B2A4A;font-weight:600;max-width:70ch;text-wrap:pretty">A custom shop can turn an RFQ email into a defensible, margin-checked quote without a catalog of repeatable products and without enterprise pricing &mdash; because the estimating logic was modeled on how the trade actually quotes, category by category, not on a generic contractor.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid #E8E4DF;border-radius:20px;background:#fff;padding:2rem;margin-bottom:1.2rem;box-shadow:0 2px 18px rgba(27,42,74,0.05)">
          <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4A5568;margin-bottom:0.6rem">The gap &mdash; why nothing off the shelf fits a custom job shop</div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 1.5rem;font-size:0.92rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.6;max-width:80ch;text-wrap:pretty">Every estimating and project-management tool on the market assumes you sell the same thing more than once. A small shop doing almost entirely custom work has no SKUs, no catalog, and no per-unit history to price against &mdash; and cannot justify seat pricing built for a hundred-person GC.</p>
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,15rem),1fr));gap:1rem">
            <div style="background:#F4F1EC;border-radius:14px;padding:1.2rem 1.3rem">
              <div style="font-size:0.58rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B6914;margin-bottom:0.55rem">Too clunky</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.86rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.5">Enterprise estimators want a fully structured takeoff before they&rsquo;ll give a number. A shop quoting off a two-paragraph email never has that.</div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:#F4F1EC;border-radius:14px;padding:1.2rem 1.3rem">
              <div style="font-size:0.58rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B6914;margin-bottom:0.55rem">Too expensive</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.86rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.5">Priced per seat for firms that quote hundreds of jobs a month. A shop quoting a few dozen can&rsquo;t make the math work.</div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:#F4F1EC;border-radius:14px;padding:1.2rem 1.3rem">
              <div style="font-size:0.58rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B6914;margin-bottom:0.55rem">Wrong assumption</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.86rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.5">They model repeatable products with thin labor. Custom fabrication is the inverse: labor dominates, and no two pieces are alike.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid #E8E4DF;border-radius:20px;background:#fff;padding:2.2rem 2rem;margin-bottom:1.2rem;box-shadow:0 2px 18px rgba(27,42,74,0.05)">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:1.6rem">
            <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4A5568">RFQ email &rarr; quote &mdash; where AI helps and where math does the work</div>
            <div style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#4A5568">AI extracts and assists. The estimate itself is deterministic math.</div>
          </div>
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr));gap:0.7rem;align-items:stretch">
            <div style="background:#F4F1EC;border-radius:14px;padding:1rem 1rem 1.1rem">
              <div style="font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;color:#4A5568;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:0.5rem">STEP 01</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.9rem;font-weight:700;color:#1B2A4A;line-height:1.25;margin-bottom:0.35rem">RFQ arrives</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.45">Prose email, a spec sheet, sometimes a sketch. No structure.</div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:#EEF2E7;border:1.5px solid #7a8a5e;border-radius:14px;padding:1rem 1rem 1.1rem;position:relative">
              <div style="position:absolute;top:-0.6rem;right:0.8rem;background:#7a8a5e;color:#fff;font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.08em;padding:0.2rem 0.55rem;border-radius:999px">AI</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;color:#4d5a38;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:0.5rem">STEP 02</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.9rem;font-weight:700;color:#1B2A4A;line-height:1.25;margin-bottom:0.35rem">Extract line items</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.45">Pull the discrete pieces out of the request in seconds, not an afternoon.</div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:#EEF2E7;border:1.5px solid #7a8a5e;border-radius:14px;padding:1rem 1rem 1.1rem;position:relative">
              <div style="position:absolute;top:-0.6rem;right:0.8rem;background:#7a8a5e;color:#fff;font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.08em;padding:0.2rem 0.55rem;border-radius:999px">AI</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;color:#4d5a38;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:0.5rem">STEP 03</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.9rem;font-weight:700;color:#1B2A4A;line-height:1.25;margin-bottom:0.35rem">Keyword-match past jobs</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.45">Surface the closest real jobs the shop has already built and been paid for.</div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:#FDF3E3;border:1.5px solid #B8922E;border-radius:14px;padding:1rem 1rem 1.1rem;position:relative">
              <div style="position:absolute;top:-0.6rem;right:0.8rem;background:#8B6914;color:#fff;font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.08em;padding:0.2rem 0.55rem;border-radius:999px">MATH</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;color:#8B6914;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:0.5rem">STEP 04</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.9rem;font-weight:700;color:#1B2A4A;line-height:1.25;margin-bottom:0.35rem">Category engine</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.45">One engine per category. Each carries its own drivers of cost and complexity.</div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:#FDF3E3;border:1.5px solid #B8922E;border-radius:14px;padding:1rem 1rem 1.1rem;position:relative">
              <div style="position:absolute;top:-0.6rem;right:0.8rem;background:#8B6914;color:#fff;font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.08em;padding:0.2rem 0.55rem;border-radius:999px">MATH</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;color:#8B6914;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:0.5rem">STEP 05</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.9rem;font-weight:700;color:#1B2A4A;line-height:1.25;margin-bottom:0.35rem">Margin check</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.45">Gross margin against this shop&rsquo;s real history, not industry averages.</div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:#1B2A4A;border-radius:14px;padding:1rem 1rem 1.1rem">
              <div style="font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;color:#B8922E;letter-spacing:0.1em;margin-bottom:0.5rem">STEP 06</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.9rem;font-weight:700;color:#FAF8F5;line-height:1.25;margin-bottom:0.35rem">Quote out</div>
              <div style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#C9CFDB;line-height:1.45">Client-ready, itemized, auditable line by line.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div style="margin-top:1.6rem;padding-top:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid #E8E4DF">
            <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4A5568;margin-bottom:0.6rem">Four engines, because one was never going to work</div>
            <p style="margin:0 0 1.1rem;font-size:0.88rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.6;max-width:80ch;text-wrap:pretty">The visible part is the extraction. The real work was cleaning years of messy job data into something comparable, then building a separate mathematical model for each category the shop actually sells &mdash; each with its own cost drivers, its own complexity multipliers, its own definition of &ldquo;done.&rdquo;</p>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.5rem">
              <span style="font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:600;color:#FAF8F5;background:#1B2A4A;padding:0.4rem 1rem;border-radius:999px">Tabletops</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:600;color:#FAF8F5;background:#1B2A4A;padding:0.4rem 1rem;border-radius:999px">Desks</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:600;color:#FAF8F5;background:#1B2A4A;padding:0.4rem 1rem;border-radius:999px">Cabinetry</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:600;color:#FAF8F5;background:#1B2A4A;padding:0.4rem 1rem;border-radius:999px">Upholstery</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,20rem),1fr));gap:1.2rem;margin-bottom:1.2rem">
          <div style="border:1px solid #E8E4DF;border-radius:20px;background:#fff;padding:1.8rem 1.8rem 2rem">
            <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B6914;margin-bottom:0.8rem">The judgment call &mdash; a cabinet through the table engine</div>
            <p style="margin:0 0 1.5rem;font-size:0.88rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.6;text-wrap:pretty">Tabletops were the base structure, so the honest test was to push a real cabinetry job through it end to end and check the output against a competitor&rsquo;s actual quote on the same work. It failed in <strong style="color:#1B2A4A">both directions at once</strong> &mdash; which is exactly what told me the architecture had to be per-category.</p>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.9rem">
              <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;padding:1.1rem 1.2rem;background:#F4F1EC;border-radius:14px;border-left:3px solid #B4483A">
                <div style="flex:none;width:5.2rem">
                  <div style="font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#B4483A;margin-bottom:0.2rem">Too low</div>
                  <div style="font-size:1.45rem;font-weight:800;color:#1B2A4A;letter-spacing:-0.035em;line-height:1">$4,400</div>
                </div>
                <div style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.5">of hardware and subbed-out parts the table engine never asks about, because a tabletop doesn&rsquo;t have slides, hinges, pulls or a finish sub.</div>
              </div>
              <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;padding:1.1rem 1.2rem;background:#F4F1EC;border-radius:14px;border-left:3px solid #8B6914">
                <div style="flex:none;width:5.2rem">
                  <div style="font-size:0.55rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B6914;margin-bottom:0.2rem">Too high</div>
                  <div style="font-size:1.45rem;font-weight:800;color:#1B2A4A;letter-spacing:-0.035em;line-height:1">3.6&times;</div>
                </div>
                <div style="font-size:0.8rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.5">on labor &mdash; 348 predicted hours against a realistic 96, because the table model reads size as complexity and can&rsquo;t see complexity <em>within</em> a piece.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p style="margin:1.4rem 0 0;font-size:0.85rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.6;text-wrap:pretty">The pricing logic held. The inputs didn&rsquo;t. The fix wasn&rsquo;t a fudge factor on top of one universal estimator &mdash; it was accepting that each category needs its own model, and naming precisely which inputs each one still owes.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="border:1px solid #E8E4DF;border-radius:20px;background:#fff;padding:1.8rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.4rem">
            <div>
              <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4A5568;margin-bottom:0.9rem">Value created</div>
              <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.65rem">
                <div style="font-size:0.84rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.5;padding-left:1.1rem;border-left:2px solid #E8E4DF">An RFQ email becomes a structured, itemized estimate in minutes instead of an afternoon of reading and guessing</div>
                <div style="font-size:0.84rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.5;padding-left:1.1rem;border-left:2px solid #E8E4DF">Years of inconsistent job records cleaned into a comparable history the estimate can actually price against</div>
                <div style="font-size:0.84rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.5;padding-left:1.1rem;border-left:2px solid #E8E4DF">Four category engines that price the way the trade prices &mdash; at a cost a small shop can carry</div>
                <div style="font-size:0.84rem;color:#4A5568;line-height:1.5;padding-left:1.1rem;border-left:2px solid #E8E4DF">Running production quotes today, with every number traceable to an input someone in the shop can argue with</div>
