    <section style="padding:5.5rem 2rem 5rem;background:#111D35;color:#FAF8F5">
      <div style="max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto">

        <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:2rem;margin-bottom:2.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <div style="font-size:5.5rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.05em;line-height:0.8;color:rgba(250,248,245,0.13);flex:none">02</div>
          <div style="flex:1;min-width:min(100%,26rem)">
            <div style="font-size:0.62rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#B8922E;margin-bottom:0.7rem">CNC &middot; Designed, built and physically test-cut, June 2026</div>
            <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.9rem,3.6vw,2.7rem);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-0.038em;line-height:1.05;margin:0 0 0.6rem;max-width:26ch">Kabbalah Wave: generative CNC from a name and a birthdate</h2>
            <p style="font-size:1rem;color:#C9CFDB;line-height:1.6;margin:0;max-width:56ch">Nothing existing takes personal identity and returns a one-of-a-kind, physically cuttable relief panel. Both the generative math and the safety net that keeps it off a machine when it isn&rsquo;t safe had to be invented.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="flex:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem;align-items:flex-start">
            <span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;background:#8B6914;color:#FAF8F5;font-size:0.76rem;font-weight:600;padding:0.6rem 1.1rem;border-radius:999px">Live engine below</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#8B9AB5">Generative Systems Designer, CNC Programmer</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="padding:1.6rem 1.8rem;background:rgba(184,146,46,0.12);border-left:4px solid #B8922E;border-radius:0 16px 16px 0;margin-bottom:1rem">
          <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#B8922E;margin-bottom:0.7rem">What it proves</div>
          <p style="margin:0;font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.5;color:#FAF8F5;font-weight:600;max-width:70ch;text-wrap:pretty">A name and a birthdate go in; CNC-ready geometry comes out, through a verification gate that has to pass before anything reaches the machine &mdash; and it went all the way to a physical cut at B10, reacted to in person on the shop floor.</p>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:0 0 3rem;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.6;color:#8B9AB5;max-width:76ch;padding-left:1.8rem;text-wrap:pretty"><strong style="color:#C9CFDB;font-weight:600">The gap:</strong> a pattern that looks good on screen isn&rsquo;t automatically safe to cut. Watertight geometry, consistent winding, a frequency the tool and material can resolve &mdash; none of it shows up in a render. Building the math was half the problem.</p>

        <div style="border:1px solid rgba(250,248,245,0.14);border-radius:20px;background:rgba(250,248,245,0.04);padding:2rem;margin-bottom:1.2rem">
