            <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#B8922E;margin-bottom:1.3rem">The judgment call &mdash; two defects invisible in preview</div>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1rem;margin-bottom:1.3rem">
              <div>
                <img src="/images/dolby/kabbalah-pattern-options.png" alt="The three pattern modes: flow, orbit, sliced" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1400/460;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;display:block;background:#1e1206" />
                <div style="font-size:0.62rem;color:#8B9AB5;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-top:0.45rem">All three modes &mdash; orbit (centre) is where the seam appeared</div>
              </div>
              <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start">
                <div style="width:9.5rem;flex:none">
                  <img src="/images/dolby/kabbalah-preview.png" alt="Rendered 24-inch square wave field derived from one set of personal inputs" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:1/1;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;display:block;background:#1e1206" />
                  <div style="font-size:0.62rem;color:#8B9AB5;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-top:0.45rem">Corrected 24&Prime; field</div>
                </div>
                <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.8rem;color:#8B9AB5;line-height:1.55;padding-top:0.2rem">The seam radiated from the centre of the orbit field, where <code style="color:#B8922E;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace">atan2</code> wraps. Quantizing spin to a whole number of arms makes the angular term jump a full cosine cycle across that branch cut &mdash; the wrap goes seamless without changing the pattern.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.85rem;color:#C9CFDB;line-height:1.6;text-wrap:pretty">Early exports looked right and weren&rsquo;t safe to cut. Orbit had that hard seam; the 3D export had its surface normals wound backwards &mdash; invisible in a render, but the kind of defect that damages a bit or warps a part. I found the actual cause of each rather than patching the symptom.</p>
          </div>

          <div style="border:1px solid rgba(250,248,245,0.14);border-radius:20px;background:rgba(250,248,245,0.04);padding:1.8rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.2rem">
            <div style="font-size:0.6rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#B8922E">The verification gate &mdash; mandatory, permanent</div>
            <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.85rem;color:#C9CFDB;line-height:1.55">That near-miss is why nothing reaches the machine unchecked. Every exported STL passes three assertions or it does not ship.</p>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem">
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.9rem;background:#0B1425;border-radius:12px;padding:0.85rem 1.1rem"><span style="width:1.4rem;height:1.4rem;border-radius:50%;background:#7a8a5e;color:#0B1425;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:800;flex:none">&#10003;</span><span style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#FAF8F5;font-weight:600">Watertight</span><code style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#8B9AB5;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;margin-left:auto">is_watertight</code></div>
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.9rem;background:#0B1425;border-radius:12px;padding:0.85rem 1.1rem"><span style="width:1.4rem;height:1.4rem;border-radius:50%;background:#7a8a5e;color:#0B1425;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:800;flex:none">&#10003;</span><span style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#FAF8F5;font-weight:600">Consistently wound</span><code style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#8B9AB5;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;margin-left:auto">is_winding_consistent</code></div>
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.9rem;background:#0B1425;border-radius:12px;padding:0.85rem 1.1rem"><span style="width:1.4rem;height:1.4rem;border-radius:50%;background:#7a8a5e;color:#0B1425;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:0.8rem;font-weight:800;flex:none">&#10003;</span><span style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#FAF8F5;font-weight:600">Positive volume</span><code style="font-size:0.7rem;color:#8B9AB5;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;margin-left:auto">volume &gt; 0</code></div>
              <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.9rem;border:1px dashed rgba(184,146,46,0.5);border-radius:12px;padding:0.85rem 1.1rem"><span style="width:1.4rem;height:1.4rem;border-radius:50%;background:#B8922E;color:#0B1425;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:0.85rem;font-weight:800;flex:none">&rarr;</span><span style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#B8922E;font-weight:700">Cleared for the machine</span></div>
